surface: two objectql test files (engine lane) and one dogfood test. They are declared in pr_body_edits for the #6367 rider. (2) protocol-duplicate-package-unprefixed-object.test.ts is left red at this head (open question 1). (3) The dogfood suite was not run in full: the 7 grep-named files plus the re-trued file ran (8 / 51 passed); the rest is main's full battery. A git grep for package-scoped view writes names only the re-trued file. (4) @objectstack/spec's suite was not run: it has no workspace dependency, so it cannot reach the gate (declared narrowing). (5) The branch was not re-merged. No file this PR touches changed on main (now 7c7741dcb4), but dispatch-gates warned STALE TREE for 3 derivation inputs. (6) The first sweep run was restarted to add --maxWorkers=2. Its build child (my own PID 15613) was left to finish, not killed. (7) The clone was deepened (git fetch --shallow-since=2026-07-14 origin main) so check-engine-split-ratio could compute. (8) The worktree was re-created on the existing branch (the round-0 cleanup had removed it). (9) PR body: not PATCHed. 18 old/new pairs are in pr_body_edits, each old_str verified to occur exactly once in the live body (byte-identical to the round-0 create). Suggested title: 'fix(lint)!: the save door refuses a list view written into a package and bound outside its closure'.",
  "tests": "Pins at a0c24ab647: lint runtime-gate.package-closure.test.ts 27/27; metadata-protocol protocol.runtime-authoring-gate.test.ts 162/162 (the #24563 block has 10 cases). Ablation (severity back to warning) through scripts/ablation-replace.mjs: \"severity: 'error'\" became \"severity: String(object) === 'ablated_24563_warning' ? 'error' : 'warning'\", anchor 1→0, blob f38af8f08988→377fdb85d3dd; lint rebuilt; ablation-dist-preflight marker present in 4 built files. Mutated: lint file 4 red / 23 green (the three refusal cases and the object-door refusal in the flow case; the CLI case checks the rule id only and stayed green); protocol block 5 red ((a)×2, (d), (e), (g)) / 5 green (the draft save, (b)×2, (c), (f)). Restore: blob == HEAD, git diff HEAD empty, rebuild, --absent from all 20 built files, tree clean; 27/27 and 162/162. Consumer sweep, each run as pnpm --filter PKG test --maxWorkers=2 under os-verify-lock.sh: lint 148/6934 passed; metadata-protocol 248 passed + 3 skipped / 20733 passed; objectql first run 445 passed, 2 failed / 8407 passed, 7 failed (6 names-in-step, re-trued → 6/6; 1 unprefixed-object, left red); rest 300/6095; runtime 423/6655; core 106/2580; metadata 63/892; platform-objects 78/1188; plugin-security 188/3754; service-automation 192/2567; service-cluster 7/105; service-datasource 45/838; cli (both projects) 474 passed, 1 skipped / 6018 passed. At a0c24ab647, objectql conformance + names-in-step + unprefixed: 25 passed, 1 failed ('a name already claimed is refused up front…': failed has 2 entries, the second 'view/ticket_views … views[0].object [list-view-object-outside-closure]'). Conformance alone was 16/16 after its re-true; before it, 6 failed under the refusal. Dogfood: the 7 grep-named files plus view-container-cross-package-default → 8 files / 51 tests passed. Control: that file without the declared dependency → 2 failed, 'expected 422 to be 200' (PUT /api/v1/meta/view/os_qa_keyed_probe?package=com.example.repairassets) and 'expected 'refused' to be 'published'' (POST /packages/com.example.repairassets/publish-drafts). That is the refusal measured through the booted REST door. Typechecks exit 0: lint (with check:test-typecheck), metadata-protocol, objectql, dogfood. P3 harness re-run (temporary, deleted): universe 119 objects, 11 views / 39 bindings, 0 outside the closure, 0 refused scoped or whole; control → errors ['list-view-object-outside-closure' ×3], advisories [].",
  "gates": "At a0c24ab647: node scripts/pm/dispatch-gates.mjs --commands --repo objectstack-ai/objectstack, no paths, 12 changed paths vs merge base c3954057f → 95 families, each run verbatim with exit captured before any pipe. The derivation warned STALE TREE: 3 derivation inputs changed on main, none a file this PR touches; not re-merged per the patch instruction. First non-zero runs, re-run after fixing their prerequisite: check-engine-split-ratio --days 90 exit 2 (shallow refusal) → deepened → exit 0; check:skill-examples exit 3 (client-react without .d.ts) → built client and client-react → exit 0. NOT MEASURED: check:dual-build-cjs-loads, exit 3 PREREQUISITE NOT MET (needs every package built), left to CI. --ran: '✓ dispatch-gates --ran: 95 derived famil(ies) accounted for — 94 run, 1 NOT-MEASURED (1 DERIVED from a recorded exit 3)', exit 0. check-adr-0087-registration --base origin/main exit 0 ('1 declared-breaking changeset(s), each carrying an ADR-0087 disposition'); check-empty-changeset --base origin/main exit 0; check-changeset-no-major --base origin/main exit 0 ('This diff introduces no `major` bump'); check:nul-bytes OK; check:cross-package-test-inputs OK; check:test-source-alias OK. Not local: test:repo and pnpm lint (CI-owned). PR check-runs on a0c24ab647 at report time: 14 success, 5 skipped, 19 in_progress, 0 failure. Test Core is expected to go red on protocol-duplicate-package-unprefixed-object.test.ts (open question 1).",
