  "pr_body_edits": [
    {
      "old_str": "Fixes #24563\n\nClause-②: yes\n\n",
      "new_str": "Fixes #24563\n\nClause-②: yes (narrowing)\n\n"
    },
    {
      "old_str": "- **A binding outside the closure is reported, never skipped.** This covers an object of a package the writing package never declared, and an object that exists nowhere. It gets one `list-view-object-outside-closure` finding at `warning`, located at the key the binding is read from (`views[0].data.object`). The hint names the remedy: declare a dependency on the package that defines the object in the `dependencies` of the writing package's manifest. That is the verdict a flow's out-of-closure trigger object gets at the same door (P2), so the write is still stored and the finding rides the 2xx `advisories`.",
      "new_str": "- **A binding outside the closure is refused, never skipped.** This covers an object of a package the writing package never declared, and an object that exists nowhere. A publish-mode write (an active save, a draft promotion, a package draft publish) answers `422 INVALID_METADATA` with one `list-view-object-outside-closure` issue at `error`, located at the key the binding is read from (`views[0].data.object`), and nothing is stored. The hint names the remedy: declare a dependency on the package that defines the object in the `dependencies` of the writing package's manifest. That is the verdict the dataset door already gives an out-of-closure base object under the same closure (P2). The flow door's advisory is unchanged. Drafts stay ungated, and a stored row is judged at its next save."
    },
    {
      "old_str": "## Read first: the declaration differs from the claim\n\nThe claim (`6271302258`) and the dispatch carry `Clause-②: no (narrowing)`. That line was written when the out-of-closure binding was expected to be refused. P2 measured a flow's out-of-closure object reference at advisory severity. The dispatch's own prohibition says that in that case \"the view gets the same advisory for the binding, and the in-closure field refusal stays as it is\". So this PR refuses nothing that was accepted before: no accept set narrows. The public surface does grow, by an optional `AuthoringRuleContext.packageScope`, an optional second argument to `validateListViewFieldRefs`, and two new exports (`LIST_VIEW_OBJECT_OUTSIDE_CLOSURE`, `ListViewFieldRefOptions`). That is `Clause-②: yes` by the definition \"does this card widen the accept set or enlarge the public surface\". So this body and the changeset declare `Clause-②: yes` at `minor`, with no `!`, no FROM / TO lines and no ADR-0087 disposition. The claim's line is the seat's to correct, or this body's if the seat rules otherwise.\n\n",
      "new_str": "## Patch round 1: refused, not advised\n\nThe seat answered the round-0 question with B (record `6273946447` on this PR) and amended the claim's line to `Clause-②: yes (narrowing)` (`6273958360` on #24563). `list-view-object-outside-closure` is now an `error`, so the door narrows: the binding the round-0 head reported is refused. The public surface still grows by an optional `AuthoringRuleContext.packageScope`, an optional second argument to `validateListViewFieldRefs`, and two exports (`LIST_VIEW_OBJECT_OUTSIDE_CLOSURE`, `ListViewFieldRefOptions`). Widen plus narrow is `Clause-②: yes (narrowing)`. The changeset is `minor` with a `!` title, FROM / TO / Fix lines and the ADR-0087 disposition `not-required (no-migration-prescription)`. Round 0's CI red (`Test Core (5/6)`, the objectql publish-drafts conformance fixture) and the consumer sweep's fixtures are re-trued in the same commit; see \"Fixtures re-trued\".\n\n"
    },
    {
      "old_str": "a binding missing from `stack.objects` is reported once per list view, at the key it was read from",
      "new_str": "a binding missing from `stack.objects` is refused once per list view (`error`), at the key it was read from"
    },
    {
      "old_str": "    - out-of-closure binding reported, `nosuch_obj` reported, and reported under an empty closure;",
      "new_str": "    - out-of-closure binding refused, `nosuch_obj` refused, and refused under an empty closure;"
    },
    {
      "old_str": "    - the flow verdict unchanged, with a stored sibling's out-of-closure list view cancelling in the differential and reported when that object is itself written;",
      "new_str": "    - the flow verdict unchanged, with a stored sibling's out-of-closure list view cancelling in the differential (a flow publish is not refused for it) and refused when that object is itself written;"
    },
    {
      "old_str": "    - (a) the active save is reported, for the stranger's object and for `nosuch_obj`;",
      "new_str": "    - (a) the active save is refused `422 INVALID_METADATA` at `views[0].data.object`, nothing stored, for the stranger's object and for `nosuch_obj`; the draft save of the same body is not gated;"
    },
    {
      "old_str": "    - (d) draft promotion: reported, and the in-closure case refused;\n    - (e) package draft publish: reported on `published[].advisories`, and the in-closure case refused;\n    - (f) a view bound to an object drafted in the same batch: no phantom report, and its fields judged.",
      "new_str": "    - (d) draft promotion: refused, nothing stored, and the in-closure case refused;\n    - (e) package draft publish: refused (`failed[0]`, `INVALID_METADATA`, the closure issue), nothing stored, and the in-closure case refused;\n    - (f) a view bound to an object drafted in the same batch: no phantom refusal, and its fields judged;\n    - (g) a stored view with the binding loads (`loaded: 1, errors: 0`); its next save into the package is refused and the row is untouched."
    },
    {
      "old_str": "- **Changeset:** `.changeset/24563-list-view-out-of-closure.md`, `@objectstack/lint` `minor`, `Clause-②: yes`.",
      "new_str": "- **Changeset:** `.changeset/24563-list-view-out-of-closure.md`, `@objectstack/lint` `minor`, `!` title, `Clause-②: yes (narrowing)`, FROM / TO / Fix lines, the stored-row sentence, and the ADR-0087 disposition `not-required (no-migration-prescription)` (`check-adr-0087-registration --base origin/main`: \"1 declared-breaking changeset(s), each carrying an ADR-0087 disposition\")."
    },
    {
      "old_str": "- After (this branch):\n  - stranger's object: `RESOLVED success=true state=active advisories=[[\"list-view-object-outside-closure\",\"warning\",\"views[0].data.object\"]]`;\n  - `nosuch_obj`: the same advisory;\n  - overlay: unchanged (`422`, and `nosuch_obj` there `200` with `advisories=[]`);\n  - `publishPackageDrafts`: `published=1` with `published[0].advisories=[[\"list-view-object-outside-closure\",\"warning\",\"views[0].data.object\"]]`;\n  - in-closure controls: unchanged.",
      "new_str": "- After (patch round 1, `a0c24ab647`), through the protocol block on the same harness:\n  - stranger's object: refused `422 INVALID_METADATA`, `issues=[[\"list-view-object-outside-closure\",\"error\",\"views[0].data.object\"]]`, no active row;\n  - `nosuch_obj`: the same refusal;\n  - overlay: unchanged (`422 list-view-field-unknown`, and `nosuch_obj` there `200` with `advisories=[]`);\n  - `publishPackageDrafts`: `success=false publishedCount=0`, `failed[0]` `INVALID_METADATA` with the closure issue;\n  - in-closure controls: unchanged.\n- After, through the booted HTTP door: the dogfood file `view-container-cross-package-default.dogfood.test.ts` (real showcase composition, REST) run with its Studio-created package declaring NO dependency answered `expected 422 to be 200` on `PUT /api/v1/meta/view/os_qa_keyed_probe?package=com.example.repairassets` and `expected 'refused' to be 'published'` on `POST /packages/com.example.repairassets/publish-drafts`. With the dependency declared it passes 4/4.\n- (Round 0, `8a295d8477`, for the record: the same probe answered `RESOLVED success=true` with the finding at `warning` in `advisories`.)"
    },
    {
      "old_str": "So the door has two verdicts today for \"an object outside the package's closure\": flow advisory, dataset refusal. Per the dispatch the view takes the flow's. The question is raised in the report.",
      "new_str": "So the door had two verdicts for \"an object outside the package's closure\": flow advisory, dataset refusal. Round 0 gave the view the flow's; patch round 1 gives it the dataset's (the seat's answer B). The flow door is unchanged."
    },
    {
      "old_str": "- Control through the same harness: the CRM lead view retargeted at `showcase_task`, under `com.example.crm`, draws 3 advisories (`list` and its two `listViews`) and 0 errors.",
      "new_str": "- Control through the same harness: the CRM lead view retargeted at `showcase_task`, under `com.example.crm`, draws 3 advisories (`list` and its two `listViews`) and 0 errors at round 0.\n- Re-run at patch round 1 (`a0c24ab647`, universe 119 objects after main added `sys_identity_email`): 11 views, 39 bindings, 0 outside the closure, 0 refused, scoped or whole. The control now draws 3 errors (`list-view-object-outside-closure` ×3) and 0 advisories."
    },
    {
      "old_str": "  - its ladder answers `error` for an unprefixed unresolved name. Package scope, out-of-closure: `[\"error:object-reference-unknown@views[0].object\"]`. That is a refusal, not the P2 verdict;",
      "new_str": "  - its ladder answers `error` for an unprefixed unresolved name but `warning` for a platform-prefixed one, and its severity is not keyed to the closure. Package scope, out-of-closure: `[\"error:object-reference-unknown@views[0].object\"]`;"
    },
    {
      "old_str": "- **G3. Falsified in part, by P2.** The out-of-closure binding is advisory and the in-closure refusal already existed, so no accept set narrows.\n  - The changeset is `minor` on the public-surface growth, with `Clause-②: yes`.\n  - There is no `!`, no FROM / TO, and no ADR-0087 marker: `check-adr-0087-registration --base origin/main` reads no breaking declaration.\n  - The Fix line is there: declare the dependency, or bind inside the closure, after which the field is judged.\n",
      "new_str": "- **G3. Held at patch round 1.** `minor`, `!` title, `Clause-②: yes (narrowing)`, FROM / TO / Fix lines (the fix: declare the dependency on the defining package in the writing package's manifest `dependencies`, or bind an object it may reach), following PR #24509's changeset. `check-adr-0087-registration --base origin/main` decides `not-required (no-migration-prescription)`: exit 0, \"1 declared-breaking changeset(s), each carrying an ADR-0087 disposition\". (Round 0 had it falsified by P2's advisory.)\n"
    },
    {
      "old_str": "## Verification\n\n",
      "new_str": "## Verification\n\n### Patch round 1 (head `a0c24ab647`)\n\n- One commit on `8a295d8477` (no merge: no file this PR touches changed on `main`, now `7c7741dcb4`).\n- Consumer sweep, every package whose tests save or publish through the gate (`git grep -l \"publishPackageDrafts\\|saveMetaItem\" -- \"packages/**/*.test.ts\"`). Each ran `pnpm --filter PKG test --maxWorkers=2` under `os-verify-lock.sh`, after the dependency closures were rebuilt:\n  - `@objectstack/lint` 148 files / 6934 tests passed;\n  - `@objectstack/metadata-protocol` 248 passed, 3 skipped / 20733 passed, 19 skipped;\n  - `@objectstack/objectql` 445 passed, 2 failed / 8407 passed, 7 failed on the first run. 6 were `protocol-duplicate-package-names-in-step.test.ts` (re-trued below: 6/6), and 1 is `protocol-duplicate-package-unprefixed-object.test.ts` \"a name already claimed…\", left red and raised as an open question (below). At `a0c24ab647` the conformance, names-in-step and unprefixed files read 25 passed, 1 failed (that one);\n  - `@objectstack/rest` 300 / 6095 passed; `@objectstack/runtime` 423 / 6655 passed; `@objectstack/core` 106 / 2580; `@objectstack/metadata` 63 / 892; `@objectstack/platform-objects` 78 / 1188; `@objectstack/plugin-security` 188 / 3754; `@objectstack/service-automation` 192 / 2567; `@objectstack/service-cluster` 7 / 105; `@objectstack/service-datasource` 45 / 838; `@objectstack/cli` (both projects) 474 passed, 1 skipped / 6018 passed;\n  - `@objectstack/dogfood`: the 7 files the grep names plus the re-trued `view-container-cross-package-default.dogfood.test.ts`, 8 files / 51 tests passed. The rest of the dogfood suite was not run locally (main's full battery runs it); a `git grep` for package-scoped view writes (`meta/view…?package=`) in `packages/qa/dogfood/test` names only the re-trued file;\n  - `@objectstack/spec` was not run: it has no workspace dependency (`pg-connection-string`, `zod`), so no spec test can reach `@objectstack/lint`. Its grep hits are prose.\n- Typechecks: `lint` (with `check:test-typecheck`), `metadata-protocol`, `objectql` and `dogfood` exit 0.\n- **Ablation** (the seat's ask), on the patch with the severity set back: `severity: 'error'` became `severity: String(object) === 'ablated_24563_warning' ? 'error' : 'warning'` through `scripts/ablation-replace.mjs` (anchor 1 → 0, blob `f38af8f08988` → `377fdb85d3dd`), lint rebuilt, marker in 4 built files.\n  - Lint file: 4 red, 23 green. The reds were the three refusal cases and the object-door refusal inside the flow case. The CLI case stayed green because it checks the rule id only.\n  - Protocol block: 5 red ((a) ×2, (d), (e), (g)), 5 green (the draft save, (b) ×2, (c), (f)). Exactly the refusal legs went red; every control held.\n  - Restore: blob == HEAD, `git diff HEAD` empty, rebuild, `--absent` from all 20 built files, tree clean; lint file 27/27, protocol file 162/162.\n  - The ablation ran on the patch's lint source (blob `f38af8f08988`, unchanged in `a0c24ab647`) before the fixture files were folded into the same commit.\n\n### Round 0\n\n"
    },
    {
      "old_str": "## Gates\n\nThese were run on the merge head `8a295d8477`, which is the PR head.\n",
      "new_str": "## Gates\n\n### Patch round 1 (head `a0c24ab647`)\n\n- `node scripts/pm/dispatch-gates.mjs --commands --repo objectstack-ai/objectstack`, no paths: 95 families from 12 changed paths against merge base `c3954057f`. Each ran verbatim with its exit code recorded before any pipe.\n  - `--ran`: \"95 derived famil(ies) accounted for — 94 run, 1 NOT-MEASURED (1 DERIVED from a recorded exit 3)\", exit 0.\n  - The derivation warned STALE TREE: 3 derivation inputs (`scripts/check-stack-collection-maps.mjs`, `scripts/engine-double-contract.pinned.json`, `scripts/platform-object-tenancy-census.json`) changed on `main` since the merge base. None is a file this PR touches, so the branch was not re-merged, per the patch instruction. CI judges the merge ref.\n- First runs that were not 0, and their re-runs:\n  - `check-engine-split-ratio --days 90` exited 2, the shallow-clone refusal. After `git fetch --shallow-since=2026-07-14 origin main` it exited 0;\n  - `check:skill-examples` exited 3 (client-react had no `.d.ts`). After building `client` and `client-react` it exited 0 (\"262 prose examples type-check\");\n  - `check:dual-build-cjs-loads` exited 3 (`PREREQUISITE NOT MET`) and is NOT MEASURED, left to CI.\n- `check-adr-0087-registration --base origin/main` exit 0 (\"1 declared-breaking changeset(s), each carrying an ADR-0087 disposition\"); `check-empty-changeset --base origin/main` exit 0; `check-changeset-no-major --base origin/main` exit 0 (\"This diff introduces no `major` bump\").\n- `check:nul-bytes`, `check:cross-package-test-inputs`, `check:test-source-alias` and `check:engine-double-contract`: OK.\n- Not local: `test:repo` and `pnpm lint` (CI-owned).\n\n### Round 0\n\nThese were run on the merge head `8a295d8477`.\n"
    },
    {
      "old_str": "- `content/docs/deployment/validating-metadata.mdx`, one sentence. Its \"That changes what a rule can **resolve**, never what it judges\" became false for this rule, so it now reads \"never which rules run\" and names the one rule that is told the closure is in force.",
      "new_str": "- `content/docs/deployment/validating-metadata.mdx`, one sentence. Its \"That changes what a rule can **resolve**, never what it judges\" became false for this rule, so it now reads \"never which rules run\" and says a list view bound outside the closure is refused.\n\n## Fixtures re-trued (patch round 1), assertions unchanged\n\nEach fixture saved or published a package's view bound outside that package's closure. Round 0 gave each an advisory: the names-in-step and dogfood cases passed, and the conformance file's advisory-free assertions went red (round 0's CI red). Under the refusal each write is refused. Each is re-trued so its view binds an object the package may reach, and no assertion is weakened.\n\n- `packages/objectql/src/publish-package-drafts-response-conformance.test.ts` (round 0's CI red, `Test Core (5/6)`). The views bound `case`, which exists nowhere in that harness. Six cases were refused under B: plain batch, probes, materializer, advisories, and two invariants. `byte-stability` passed only vacuously (an empty `published[]`). `viewBody` now binds `sys_metadata`, a platform object the harness registers, with its declared `id` column. The view element stays advisory-free beside the flow that carries the advisory. 16/16.\n- `packages/objectql/src/protocol-duplicate-package-names-in-step.test.ts`. The source package saved views of a third package's objects (`dupext_account.board`, `dupsrc_ext.board`) without declaring it. The source now declares `dependencies: { [R]: '*' }`. The objects stay outside the package, which is what \"a view item of an object outside the package keeps its name\" pins, and the copy inherits the declaration with the manifest. 6/6.\n- `packages/qa/dogfood/test/view-container-cross-package-default.dogfood.test.ts`. The Studio-created `com.example.repairassets` saved containers for `showcase_task` without declaring the showcase. Its `POST /packages` manifest now declares `dependencies: { [SHOWCASE]: '*' }`. The container is still for an object another package ships, which is the test's subject. 4/4, and without the declaration it reads `422` / `refused` (P1 above).\n\nThese are three more files outside the claim's surface: the engine lane (`packages/objectql`) and `packages/qa/dogfood`. The seat adds them to the rider note on #6367.\n\n**Not re-trued (open question in the report):** `packages/objectql/src/protocol-duplicate-package-unprefixed-object.test.ts`, \"a name already claimed is refused up front, at the object, naming the rename\". There the SOURCE's view (`ticket_views`, bound to its own `ticket`) is inside its closure. The refused object copy leaves the COPY's view bound to the source's `ticket`, outside the copy's closure, and that copy is now refused: `failed` = the `ticket` object refusal plus `view/ticket_views … views[0].object [list-view-object-outside-closure]`, against the asserted length 1. No fixture change re-trues it. It needs either the assertion re-pinned to the two refusals or a `duplicatePackage` change (engine lane, `protocol.ts`), so it is red at this head."
